<title>FRANCE: EU cuts wheat export refund to Alpine states.</title>
<headline>EU cuts wheat export refund to Alpine states.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee cut the standing refund for wheat exports to Switzerland and Liechtenstein on Thursday to three Ecus per tonne from 6.50 Ecus, the French cereals office ONIC said.</p>
<p>The committee, however, maintained the refund for barley and rye exports to these destinations at 17.50 Ecus per tonne and 21 Ecus per tonne respectively.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
